---
description: Elysia t. schemas must be inline per route — never extracted and reused
globs: routes/**/*.js
alwaysApply: false
---

# Inline Elysia route schemas

Put `t.Object` / `t.String` / `t.Numeric` **directly** on that route’s `body`, `params`, or `query`. Do not define a schema at the top of the file (or in a helper) and pass it into two routes.

```js
// ❌ BAD — extracted and reused
const customerBody = t.Object({
    full_name: t.String({ minLength: 1, maxLength: 128 }),
});

app.post("/", addCustomer, { body: customerBody })
   .patch("/", updateCustomer, { body: customerBody });

// ❌ BAD — shared field schema
const phone = t.String({ pattern: "^\\+?[0-9]{10,13}$" });
app.post("/", add, { body: t.Object({ phones: t.Array(phone) }) })
   .patch("/", update, { body: t.Object({ phones: t.Array(phone) }) });

// ✅ GOOD — each route owns a full inline schema (duplicate fields if needed)
app.post("/", addCustomer, {
    body: t.Object({
        full_name: t.String({ minLength: 1, maxLength: 128 }),
        phones: t.Optional(t.Array(t.String({ pattern: "^\\+?[0-9]{10,13}$" }))),
    }),
}).patch("/", updateCustomer, {
    body: t.Object({
        id: t.Numeric({ minimum: 1 }),
        full_name: t.String({ minLength: 1, maxLength: 128 }),
        phones: t.Optional(t.Array(t.String({ pattern: "^\\+?[0-9]{10,13}$" }))),
    }),
});
```
